/P 130 0 R
/E (Accurate water-body detection is essential for environmental monitoring, flood assessment, coastal management, and climate-change studies. However, identifying water from satellite imagery can be challenging due to clouds, shadows, seasonal variations, and the complexity of different landscapes.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (To address this challenge, this project uses a U-Net deep learning model trained on 12-channel multi-source satellite data. The input data combines spectral information from Sentinel-2/Landsat imagery with elevation models, land-cover maps, quality assessment layers, and historical water occurrence information.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
